      "created_at": "2018-02-13T00:27:01.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Great questions!&nbsp; :D</p><p>I'm not sure why you would ever remove a hinder with a boost in combat assuming they are both one time sort of effects.&nbsp; I guess if you did not want the GM to play it during a critical moment you could get rid of it with a boost.&nbsp; If the hinder was permanent I could see spending a boost getting rid of it.&nbsp; in your pipe example that would mean destroying the pipe I guess...</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
